<!--
  Client (right-click titlebar) menu, ported from ~/.fluxbox/windowmenu.

  CORRECTION vs. openbox-port-plan.md gap #4: "client-menu" is not actually
  data-driven in this Openbox (3.6.1) the way root-menu/session-menu/etc are.
  A <menu id="client-menu"> block here is silently ignored - verified live:
  defining one with a different item list still popped Openbox's own
  hardcoded menu (Send to desktop / Layer / Restore / Move / Resize /
  Iconify / Maximize / Roll up-down / Un-Decorate / Close). So there is
  nothing to author for the parts windowmenu already covered
  (shade->"Roll up/down", maximize, iconify, close, [sendto]->"Send to
  desktop", [layer]->"Layer" - all present automatically, no menu.xml
  entry needed or possible.

  What's genuinely gone, confirmed by that same built-in list:
    - [stick] (sticky/omnipresent toggle) - no equivalent item exists in
      Openbox's built-in client-menu at all (bindable via ToggleOmnipresent
      as a mouse/key action instead - see rc.xml's AllDesktops context)
      but not reachable from this menu).
    - [alpha] (opacity slider) - gap #4, no built-in equivalent.
    - [extramenus] - gap #4, no built-in equivalent.
-->


</openbox_menu>
